  "routeSelection": {
    "route": "Pedagogy and Educational Sciences",
    "selectionRule": "broad-academic-identity",
    "basis": "The generic 180-EC Pedagogical Sciences target does not name a route. The 2026–27 appendix offers Pedagogy/Educational Sciences and Orthopedagogy; the former broadly retains upbringing, education, family, social development and educational policy, whereas the latter is more specialised in diagnostics and intervention. The four-year primary-school teacher double degree is not the ordinary bachelor route. This choice precedes UCR course selection."
  },
  "progression": [
    "Year one consists of twelve 5 EC units in pedagogy, development, schooling, sociology and research. The faculty study advice threshold is 45 EC. Ordinary completion of the first year supports the later sequence.",
    "Year two contains 35 EC common and 25 EC route work, including the shared 5 EC research practicum. Its two linked Academic Learning Communities assignments are a requirement within those 5 EC, without separate credits.",
    "Year three contains 15 EC common, 5 EC of selected workshops, 10 EC thesis and 30 EC minor. The two previously selected workshops are separately listed in the same option group and have no published earlier-course prerequisite. The adopted appendix requires all year-one EC and 40 EC from years two or three before the thesis, satisfied by the normal progression. The internship is 5 EC and supervised practice."
  ]
}
